      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "xmldb",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tMain ideas are NON-Relational DB ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tHopefully good replacement for folks using ORM, not replacement for use of sql useage",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tTakes XMLSchema to define DB layout",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tFor each type – create folder, and for each instance, separate file",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tAt least one back-end impl would do this – idea is multiple virtual backend impl eingnes – one that might back end to storing on relational db via sql, etc.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tObjects have opaque ids automatically, and can be referenced (even if not in the xml schema)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tMust support transactions (objects)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tEventually support XML Schema validation, but hard to use COTS validator given disparate file model – but not impossible – given sax parsing validators. Just that would be very very costly (or I need a clever trick – like isolating TRANSACTIOSN and just validating THEM somehow)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tAPI COULD be 2 tiered",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tMap-based (like ADO) – Records are assocations of fieldname -> memory::variant",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tAnd have second API based on this, that generates C++ structs from schema, and automatically maps to that map / assoc list API.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tThen EXAMPLE",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\t User u;",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tU.x = ‘3’;",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tDb.Add (U);",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
